# The Python packages the build needs beyond the HzL compiler's own, as
# ranges. This is the hand-edited input: `make lock` resolves it, together
# with hzl-compiler/pyproject.toml and its dev extras, into
# requirements-dev.txt, which pins every package with its hashes and is what
# `make venv` installs. Edit this file, run `make lock`, commit both.
#
# The compiler itself is not listed: it is installed editable by `make venv`
# after the lock, without its dependencies, which the lock already holds.

# Installed from the lock so that the venv's pip and the build backend of the
# editable compiler (built without isolation) are hash-checked too.
pip
setuptools>=77

